    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6833A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to providing special\nballots for emergency responders\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo enable first responders to vote in an election during a state\ndeclared emergency\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nAdds a new section 11-308 to the election law creating special ballots\nfor emergency responders.\n\n§ 1 - allows registered voters who serve as emergency responders\nduring an emergency declared by the Governor or court of competent\njurisdiction to apply for a special ballot at any time prior to any\nelection regardless of absentee ballot deadlines.\n\n§ 2 - Emergency responders may utilize an absentee ballot application\nto request the special or may file a written statement that they are\nunable to appear at the polling place on the day of election due to\nduties as emergency responder. Boards of elections shall provide\nballot immediately upon request and may utilize overnight delivery.\nBallots may also be transmitted by facsimile or electronic transfer in\nsame format as military ballots.\n\n§ 3 - Cast ballots may be delivered to any board of elections office\nin the state or to any poll site no later than close of polls that\nElection Day.\n\n§ 4 - Board of elections shall assist emergency responders to ensure\nthe enfranchisement of the emergency responders.\n\n§ 5 - Ballots received by boards of elections from voters of another\njurisdiction shall time and date stamp and forward immediately to the\nvoters' board of election. Ballots will be considered timely if time\nstamp of first receiving board is timely. Ballots shall be cast and\ncanvassed according to same provision of absentee, military and\nspecial ballot (ELN § 9-209) and if not in standard appearance shall\nbe handled same as military ballots and request (ELN § 10-125).\n\n§ 6 - Emergency responders shall include all persons called upon to\nprovide emergency support, relief or other services during a declared\ndisaster, including, but not limited to, medical personnel, military\npersonnel, utility company or similar contract employees, fire\ndepartment personnel, police department personnel, local and state\nemergency management personnel, and other state and local government\nemployees providing response services.\n\n§ 7 - State board of elections shall develop and distribute sample\nforms and procedure to local boards of elections to effectuate this\nact.\n\n§ 8 - provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill provides emergency responders access to special ballots\nwhich can be returned to any board of elections and routed to the\nresponder's appropriate board. This legislation requires all boards of\nelections to provide assistance to responders in the application and\n\nballot return process. It authorizes ballot delivery processes to\ncommensurate to those available military voters.\n\nThis bill provides emergency responders access to special ballots so\nthat they will not lose their right to vote on account of service in\nresponse to an emergency.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately\n",
